Ritemark Store Compliance: no external software acquisition promotion
Sprint 126 (R4): Microsoft Store certification finding 10.1.5 — Source Control
offered "Download Git for Windows" linking to git-scm.com. VS Code renders a
welcome-view line as a full-width primary Button when the line parses to
exactly one link and nothing else (viewPane.ts), so the flagged element was a
large blue call-to-action.

Two surfaces change, and Ritemark now informs without offering:

  1. extensions/git/package.nls.json — the three scm.missing.* strings lose
     their bare download-link line. No line is left that parses to a single
     link, so nothing renders as a button. The explanation and the reload /
     troubleshoot commands stay. All three are gated on `git.missing`, so an
     installed Git is untouched by construction.

  2. gettingStarted.ts launch checks — "Ritemark needs Git." and "Ritemark
     needs Node." keep their status lines and lose "Click here to install".
     The Node one was not flagged; it is the identical construct, and fixing
     only what was reported would leave the same exposure for the next round.

Applies after 001, which owns the launch-check list itself.

Note: Visual Studio Code ships in the Microsoft Store with the same button,
so this is not evidence that mentioning Git acquisition is categorically
forbidden. The resubmission describes what changed, not a policy reading.
